23:52:27:720 [ 7576] | INFO  | [MGPU Bridge] [MGPU][R63] DEPTH TRANSPORT f=4815 mode=1 (TRANSPORTED AND BOUND) | producer: valid=4819 invalid=0 size-rejected=0, arm held 0 frame(s) | consumer: seals seen valid=3654 invalid=0 contract mismatches=0 | region 3840x2160 fmt=41 pitch=15360 bytes=33177600 at slot offset 33178112 of 95846912. INVALID IS NOT AN ERROR: ReShade unbinds depth in menus and scene changes, and R61 established that shipping the zeros it leaves behind would hand the model a false flat plane. An invalid frame carries the colour and says so. WHAT WOULD BE AN ERROR is contract mismatches above zero, or valid staying at zero once you are in gameplay - that means the tap is not feeding us. 100.0% of sealed frames carried depth. | GPU 1: unpacked=3560 bound=3288 skipped=0, DepthInverted=1, flag disagreements=0 (the seal crossed the adapter and the slot flag did not, so any disagreement between them is real). BOUND vs SKIPPED IS THE R61 TEST: skipped counts frames where ReShade had no depth and the model was given NONE rather than the previous frame's - open a menu mid-stream and this must move.
23:52:27:721 [ 7576] | INFO  | [MGPU Bridge] [MGPU][R78] MVEC TRANSPORT f=4815 mode=3 REAL | producer: copies=3018 missing=1801 size-rejected=0 lock-skipped=0, arm held 239 frame(s) | consumer: seals seen valid=3013 invalid=641 contract mismatches=0 flag disagreements=9 | region 2560x1440 fmt=10 pitch=20480 bytes=29491200 at slot offset 66355712 of 95846912 | GPU 1: unpacked=3013 bound=3009 skipped=279, scale=(2560.000, 1440.000). 82.5% of sealed frames carried vectors. COPIES IS THE ONE TO WATCH: it counts frames where the bind hook fired and a copy was recorded. If it stays at zero the probe published a handle nobody binds, and MVec never reaches the model whatever the rest of this line says. SKIPPED IS NOT AN ERROR - it counts frames with no vectors, which is what a menu looks like, and those frames are handed NONE rather than the last frame's motion.
23:52:27:721 [ 7576] | INFO  | [MGPU Bridge] [MGPU][R87] MVEC FRAME ALIGNMENT f=4815 | evaluates=3288 | elapsed 1=3017 2=2 3=2 4=11 5=35 6=58 7=89 8+=74 | worst=9 | 91.76% at 1. A motion vector describes ONE game frame; NR reprojects by whatever it is handed. When the frame NR blends against is older than one, history lands SHORT by this factor - zero error at rest, growing with speed, and no constant MVecScale can fix it. The scale is multiplied by this per evaluate. IF THIS LINE IS FLAT AT 1 AND THE ARTEFACT IS UNCHANGED, PACING IS ELIMINATED and what remains is units or sign. P4.1's skipped-frame counter predicts about 99.5% at 1, so a materially lower figure here is a desync no counter has shown us.
