23:52:37:543 [ 7576] | INFO  | [MGPU Bridge] [MGPU][R78] MVEC TRANSPORT f=5115 mode=3 REAL | producer: copies=3318 missing=1801 size-rejected=0 lock-skipped=0, arm held 239 frame(s) | consumer: seals seen valid=3313 invalid=641 contract mismatches=0 flag disagreements=9 | region 2560x1440 fmt=10 pitch=20480 bytes=29491200 at slot offset 66355712 of 95846912 | GPU 1: unpacked=3313 bound=3309 skipped=279, scale=(2560.000, 1440.000). 83.8% of sealed frames carried vectors. COPIES IS THE ONE TO WATCH: it counts frames where the bind hook fired and a copy was recorded. If it stays at zero the probe published a handle nobody binds, and MVec never reaches the model whatever the rest of this line says. SKIPPED IS NOT AN ERROR - it counts frames with no vectors, which is what a menu looks like, and those frames are handed NONE rather than the last frame's motion.
23:52:37:543 [ 7576] | INFO  | [MGPU Bridge] [MGPU][R87] MVEC FRAME ALIGNMENT f=5115 | evaluates=3588 | elapsed 1=3317 2=2 3=2 4=11 5=35 6=58 7=89 8+=74 | worst=9 | 92.45% at 1. A motion vector describes ONE game frame; NR reprojects by whatever it is handed. When the frame NR blends against is older than one, history lands SHORT by this factor - zero error at rest, growing with speed, and no constant MVecScale can fix it. The scale is multiplied by this per evaluate. IF THIS LINE IS FLAT AT 1 AND THE ARTEFACT IS UNCHANGED, PACING IS ELIMINATED and what remains is units or sign. P4.1's skipped-frame counter predicts about 99.5% at 1, so a materially lower figure here is a desync no counter has shown us.
